* solid pour, conv grid pitch 0.315789 mm, plane nhinc 9, trace 15x9 r2, f 100 Hz
* FastHenry deck written by pour_decks.py -- OpenSim pour loop (ExtractionTests.AReturnThroughAPour_GoesRoundASlot)
.units mm
.default sigma=58000
* return pour: uniform plane, corner nodes half a cell inside the 12 x 6 mm outline so the
* node cells tile the pour exactly; pitch 0.315789474 mm, 38 x 19 nodes
Gpour x1=-2.84210526316 y1=-2.84210526316 z1=-0.0175
+ x2=8.84210526316 y2=-2.84210526316 z2=-0.0175
+ x3=8.84210526316 y3=2.84210526316 z3=-0.0175
+ thick=0.035 seg1=37 seg2=18 sigma=58000
+ nhinc=9 rh=2
+ nps (0,0,-0.0175)
+ npe (6,0,-0.0175)
* the trace (one segment: its current is the same along its whole length)
Ns x=0 y=0 z=0.335
Ne x=6 y=0 z=0.335
Etr Ns Ne w=0.4 h=0.035 nwinc=15 nhinc=9 rw=2 rh=2
* far end shorted ideally to the plane node under it; port from the trace start to the plane under it
.equiv Ne npe
.external Ns nps loop
.freq fmin=100 fmax=100 ndec=1
.end
